# E2E Testing (Playwright)

## Structure

```
e2e/
├── fixtures.ts           # Test fixtures (loginAs, authenticated)
├── login.spec.ts         # Login page tests
├── navigation.spec.ts    # Routing, sidebar
├── theme.spec.ts         # Theme switching
├── accessibility.spec.ts # a11y checks
└── results/              # Reports (gitignored)
```

Config: `playwright.config.ts` (root).

## Commands

```bash
npm run e2e                # All tests (headless)
npm run e2e:headed         # With visible browser
npm run e2e:ui             # Playwright UI mode (interactive)
npm run e2e:chromium       # Chromium only
npm run e2e:report         # Open HTML report
```

## Fixtures

```typescript
import { test, expect } from "./fixtures";

test("with auth", async ({ authenticated }) => {
  // authenticated — Page with localStorage credentials
  await expect(authenticated.getByText("Chats")).toBeVisible();
});

test("login flow", async ({ page, loginAs }) => {
  await loginAs("user@example.com", "password", "https://zulip.example.com");
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/stream\//);
});
```

## Writing E2E tests

### Locators (priority)

1. `getByRole("button", { name: "Login" })` — best: semantic
2. `getByText("Messenger")` — good: visible text
3. `getByPlaceholder("Message...")` — good: for inputs
4. `getByTestId("chat-list")` — fallback: data-testid
5. `locator(".css-class")` — avoid: brittle

### Assertions

```typescript
await expect(page.getByText("Loading")).toBeHidden();
await expect(page.getByRole("feed")).toBeVisible();
await page.waitForURL(/\/stream\//);
await page.waitForResponse(/\/api\/v1\/messages/);
```

### Page Object (for complex tests)

```typescript
class ChatPage {
  constructor(private page: Page) {}

  async sendMessage(text: string) {
    await this.page.getByPlaceholder(/message/i).fill(text);
    await this.page.getByRole("button", { name: /send/i }).click();
  }

  async expectMessage(text: string) {
    await expect(this.page.getByText(text)).toBeVisible();
  }
}
```

## Browsers

| Project | Browser | Use case |
